{% icon id="banknote" size=32 /%}Storage full of loot you never wear? The Sell stored equipment {% term id="plugin" %}plugin{% /term %} sells loose equipment and gems from your storage, a few at a time.

Use it when your storage fills up with equipment and gems you don't need.

## How it works {% #how-it-works %}

1. After your bot signs in, it waits the number of minutes in **Minutes to wait after login before selling**, plus up to 3 minutes more.
2. It reads the equipment and the gems in your storage.
3. It sells up to **Items sold per run** items, one at a time, with a short pause between sales. Equipment comes first, then gems. It reads only the storage you ticked something for.
4. It waits about 5 minutes, then starts again at step 2.

Your {% term id="log" %}log{% /term %} shows how many pieces of equipment and how many gems each round sold. If you tick no colour and turn gems off, the plugin has nothing to sell. It says so in the log and in its status, and it does not run.

## What the bot sells and keeps {% #what-it-sells %}

The bot sells the equipment colours you tick, and loose gems if you leave **Sell loose gems** on. Each colour covers the normal pieces and the hero pieces of that rarity.

| Setting | Game rarity | Sold by default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Grey (Ordinary) | Common | Yes |
| Green (Rare) | Rare | Yes |
| Purple (Epic) | Epic | No |
| Orange (Legendary) | Legendary | No |
| Red (Unique) | Unique | No |
| Relic | Relic | No |

The bot never sells:

- Any piece of equipment or any gem that belongs to a set, whatever colours you tick.
- Equipment of a colour you did not tick.

The bot sells only from storage.

{% aside type="caution" id="sales-are-final" %}
A sale cannot be undone. Before you turn the plugin on, check your storage and your colour ticks. Every loose piece of a ticked colour gets sold, new pieces included. Leave purple, orange, red and relic unticked unless you are sure. Red (Unique) is our best guess for the game's Unique rarity, so check a piece's colour in the game first.
{% /aside %}

## Settings {% #settings %}

{% settings plugin="sellStoredEquipment" /%}

**Minutes to wait after login before selling** sets how long the bot waits after it signs in before the first sale. It takes whole minutes, from 1 to 60.

**Items sold per run** is how many items one round sells. It takes a whole number from 1 to 50.

**Equipment colours to sell** has one box for each colour. Grey and green are ticked at first, and purple, orange, red and relic are not. **Sell loose gems** is ticked at first.

## Tips and limits {% #tips %}

- The plugin has no list of single items to keep. Every loose piece of a ticked colour is for sale.
- Turn the plugin off when you want to keep new loot for a while.

## Related errors {% #errors %}

If a number is outside its range when you save, the app shows [PLUGIN_OPTION_RANGE](/errors/#plugin-option-range). If it is not a whole number, the app shows [PLUGIN_OPTION_STEP](/errors/#plugin-option-step).
